    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "An update is available for jmc.\nThis update affects Rocky Linux 9.\nA Common Vulnerability Scoring System (CVSS) base score, which gives a detailed severity rating, is available for each vulnerability from the CVE list",
        "title": "Topic"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "JDK Mission Control is a powerful profiler for HotSpot JVMs and has an advanced set of tools that enables efficient and detailed analysis of the extensive data collected by JDK Flight Recorder. The tool chain enables developers and administrators to collect and analyze data from Java applications running locally or deployed in production environments.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* lz4-java: lz4-java: Information Disclosure via Insufficient Output Buffer Clearing (CVE-2025-66566)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n\nThis advisory is provided by Ctrl IQ, Inc for Rocky Linux systems. For more information about CIQ security practices, visit https://ciq.com/security.",
        "title": "Description"
      },
      {
